],"metadata":{"id":"beRrZCGUAJYm"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# **Project Summary -**"],"metadata":{"id":"FJNUwmbgGyua"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["This project focuses on the exploratory data analysis of MediBuddy’s health insurance dataset to understand how different personal and medical factors influence insurance charges. The dataset was created by merging two files containing health details such as age, gender, and BMI along with personal information like number of dependents, smoking habits, and region. The data was cleaned to remove inconsistencies and ensure accuracy before performing analysis. Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) techniques were applied to identify trends and relationships between variables affecting insurance costs. The study reveals that factors such as age, BMI, smoking habits, and number of dependents play a significant role in determining medical expenses. Through graphical and statistical analysis, meaningful insights were obtained that can help the company improve decision-making, optimize premium pricing, and design better healthcare policies for customers.\n","\n","• The dataset was cleaned and prepared to ensure reliable analysis.\n","\n","• Age shows a positive relationship with insurance charges, with older individuals incurring higher medical costs.\n","\n","• BMI has a noticeable impact on insurance claims, where higher BMI values result in increased expenses.\n","\n","• Smoking is the most influential factor affecting insurance cost, with smokers having significantly higher charges.\n","\n","• The number of dependents moderately affects insurance expenses, as family coverage increases claim amounts.\n","\n","• Regional variations exist, indicating lifestyle and healthcare cost differences across locations.\n","\n","• Data visualization techniques were used to identify patterns and support observations.\n","\n","The analysis demonstrates that healthcare insurance costs are strongly influenced by personal health conditions and lifestyle choices. Factors such as age, BMI, and smoking habits play a major role in determining insurance claims. The insights gained from this project can help MediBuddy design risk-based insurance policies, improve premium estimation, and promote healthier lifestyles among customers. Overall, the project highlights the importance of data-driven decision-making in the healthcare insurance industry."],"metadata":{"id":"F6v_1wHtG2nS"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# **GitHub Link -**"],"metadata":{"id":"w6K7xa23Elo4"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["https://github.com/adityathakur26/MediBuddy-Insurance-Data-Analysis-EDA-Project-"],"metadata":{"id":"h1o69JH3Eqqn"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# **Problem Statement**\n"],"metadata":{"id":"yQaldy8SH6Dl"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["MediBuddy provides healthcare and insurance services to a large and diverse customer base. However, medical insurance claims vary significantly depending on factors such as age, BMI, smoking habits, location, and number of dependents. Understanding how these factors affect insurance costs is crucial for designing effective insurance policies and minimizing financial risk.\n","\n","The problem addressed in this project is to analyze customer data to identify key variables influencing insurance charges and to determine whether demographic and lifestyle attributes significantly impact medical expenses. The analysis aims to help MediBuddy make informed business decisions related to policy pricing, customer segmentation, and risk management."],"metadata":{"id":"DpeJGUA3kjGy"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### **Define Your Business Objective?**"],"metadata":{"id":"PH-0ReGfmX4f"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["The main objective of this project is to perform exploratory data analysis on MediBuddy’s insurance dataset to gain insights into customer behavior and healthcare costs. The analysis aims to:\n","\n","Identify key factors affecting insurance 