## 3. Will the gained insights help creating a positive business impact?\n","Are there any insights that lead to negative growth? Justify with specific reason."],"metadata":{"id":"JMzcOPDDphqR"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Region alone should not determine pricing, but minor regional adjustments may be applied."],"metadata":{"id":"R4Ka1PC2phqR"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Chart - 11"],"metadata":{"id":"x-EpHcCOp1ci"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Chart - 11 visualization code\n","df[\"children\"].value_counts().plot(kind=\"bar\")\n","plt.title(\"Children Count\")\n","plt.show()\n"],"metadata":{"id":"mAQTIvtqp1cj"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 1. Why did you pick the specific chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"X_VqEhTip1ck"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["This chart was selected to understand the distribution of dependents among policyholders. The number of children covered under an insurance policy plays an important role in determining healthcare usage and claim frequency. By analyzing how many dependents most customers have, we can better understand family size patterns and their potential impact on insurance planning."],"metadata":{"id":"-vsMzt_np1ck"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 2. What is/are the insight(s) found from the chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"8zGJKyg5p1ck"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["The chart shows that the majority of customers have 0 to 2 children, while very few customers have more than two dependents. This indicates that most policyholders belong to small or nuclear families. The number of customers with a high number of dependents is comparatively low."],"metadata":{"id":"ZYdMsrqVp1ck"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 3. Will the gained insights help creating a positive business impact?\n","Are there any insights that lead to negative growth? Justify with specific reason."],"metadata":{"id":"PVzmfK_Ep1ck"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["This insight is helpful for MediBuddy in designing family-oriented insurance plans. Since most customers have fewer dependents, the company can focus on affordable family coverage plans for small families. It also helps in estimating claim frequency and structuring coverage limits accordingly. Understanding dependent distribution ensures better pricing strategies and optimized family insurance products."],"metadata":{"id":"druuKYZpp1ck"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Chart - 12"],"metadata":{"id":"n3dbpmDWp1ck"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Chart - 12 visualization code\n","df.groupby(\"children\")[\"charges in INR\"].mean().plot(kind=\"bar\")\n","plt.title(\"Children vs Charges\")\n","plt.show()\n"],"metadata":{"id":"bwevp1tKp1ck"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 1. Why did you pick the specific chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"ylSl6qgtp1ck"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["This chart was chosen to analyze whether the number of dependents has any influence on insurance costs. Since dependents increase the probability of medical visits and claims, it is important to understand how insurance charges vary with family size."],"metadata":{"id":"m2xqNkiQp1ck"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 2. What is/are the insight(s) found from the chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"ZWILFDl5p1ck"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["The chart clearly shows that insurance charges increase as the number of children increases. Customers with more dependents tend to have higher medical expenses compared to those with fewer or no children. This trend indicates that family size directly impacts healthcare utilization."],"metadata":{"id":"x-lUsV2mp1ck"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 3. Will the gained insights help creating a positive business impact?\n","Are there any insights that lead to negative growth? Justify with specific reason."],"metadata":{"id":"M7G43BXep1ck"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["This insight is very useful for pricing insurance policies. MediBuddy can design tier-based family plans, where premiums increase based on the number of dependents. It also helps the company predict future claim amounts more accurately and manage financial risk effectively. This analysis supports fair and logical premium calculation for family insurance policies."],"metadata":{"id":"5wwDJXsLp1cl"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Chart - 13"],"metadata":{"id":"Ag9LCva-p1cl"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Creating age groups\n","df[\"Age_Group\"] = pd.cut(\n","    df[\"age\"],\n","    bins=[18, 30, 45, 60, 80],\n","    labels=[\"18-30\", \"31-45\", \"46-60\", \"60+\"]\n",")\n","\n","# Plotting\n","df.groupby(\"Age_Group\")[\"charges in INR\"].mean().plot(kind=\"bar\")\n","\n","plt.title(\"Age Group vs Insurance Charges\")\n","plt.xlabel(\"Age Group\")\n","plt.ylabel(\"Average Insurance Charges\")\n","plt.show()\n"],"metadata":{"id":"EUfxeq9-p1cl"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 1. Why did you pick the specific chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"E6MkPsBcp1cl"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["This chart was selected to understand how insurance charges vary across different age groups rather than individual ages. Grouping customers into age categories makes the analysis more meaningful and easier to interpret from a business perspective. It helps in identifying which age group contributes most to insurance claims.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"V22bRsFWp1cl"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 2. What is/are the insight(s) found from the chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"2cELzS2fp1cl"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["The chart shows that insurance charges increase as age increases.\n","Customers in the 18–30 age group have the lowest insurance costs, while customers in the 46–60 and 60+ age groups incur significantly higher medical expenses. This indicates that age is directly proportional to insurance risk."],"metadata":{"id":"ozQPc2_Ip1cl"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 3. Will the gained insights help creating a positive business impact?\n","Are there any insights that lead to negative growth? Justify with specific reason."],"metadata":{"id":"3MPXvC8up1cl"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["This insight is highly valuable for MediBuddy’s pricing strategy. It helps the company:\n","\n","Design age-based premium slabs\n","\n","Predict higher medical costs for older customers\n","\n","Offer preventive healthcare plans for younger age groups\n","\n","Reduce financial risk by adjusting coverage limits for senior customers\n","\n","Overall, this chart supports risk-based policy pricing and better decision-making."],"metadata":{"id":"GL8l1tdLp1cl"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Chart - 14 - Correlation Heatmap"],"metadata":{"id":"NC_X3p0fY2L0"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Correlation Heatmap visualization code\n","plt.figure(figsize=(8,6))\n","numeric_df = df.select_dtypes(include=['int64', 'float64'])\n","sns.heatmap(numeric_df.corr(), annot=True, cmap=\"coolwarm\")\n","plt.title(\"Correlation Heatmap\")\n","plt.show()\n"],"metadata":{"id":"xyC9zolEZNRQ"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 1. Why did you pick the specific chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"UV0SzAkaZNRQ"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["The correlation heatmap was selected to understand the relationships between numerical variables such as age, BMI, number of children, and insurance charges. This chart helps in identifying which factors have the strongest influence on medical expenses and how different variables are related to each other."],"metadata":{"id":"DVPuT8LYZNRQ"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 2. What is/are the insight(s) found from the chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"YPEH6qLeZNRQ"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["The heatmap shows a strong positive correlation between insurance charges and age, BMI, and smoking status. This means that as age or BMI increases, insurance costs also tend to increase. On the other hand, variables such as gender and region show very weak correlation with insurance charges."],"metadata":{"id":"bfSqtnDqZNRR"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Chart - 15 - Pair Plot"],"metadata":{"id":"q29F0dvdveiT"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Pair Plot visualization code\n","sns.pairplot(df)\n","plt.show()\n"],"metadata":{"id":"o58-TEIhveiU"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 1. Why did you pick the specific chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"EXh0U9oCveiU"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["The pair plot was selected to understand the overall relationship between multiple numerical variables at once. Unlike single charts, a pair plot allows visual comparison of all important variables such as age, BMI, children, and insurance charges in one view. It helps in identifying trends, correlations, and outliers efficiently."],"metadata":{"id":"eMmPjTByveiU"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 2. What is/are the insight(s) found from the chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"22aHeOlLveiV"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["From the pair plot, it can be observed that:\n","\n","Insurance charges increase with age and BMI.\n","\n","Customers with higher BMI tend to have higher medical expenses.\n","\n","The relationship between age and charges shows a positive trend.\n","\n","The number of children has a moderate impact on insurance cost.\n","\n","Some outliers exist, representing high-cost customers with extreme values.\n","\n","Overall, the pair plot clearly shows that health-related factors have a stronger influence on insurance charges than demographic factors."],"metadata":{"id":"uPQ8RGwHveiV"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## **5. Solution to Business Objective**"],"metadata":{"id":"JcMwzZxoAimU"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### What do you suggest the client to achieve Business Objective ?\n","Explain Briefly."],"metadata":{"id":"8G2x9gOozGDZ"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["To achieve the business objective, MediBuddy should focus on risk-based insurance pricing using customer health and lifestyle data. Based on the analysis, the company should:\n","\n","Use age and BMI as primary factors for premium calculation\n","\n","Apply higher premiums for smokers due to higher medical risk\n","\n","Introduce discounts for healthy customers with normal BMI\n","\n","Offer family-based policies based on number of dependents\n","\n","Use data-driven insights to reduce claim losses and improve profitability\n","\n","By applying these strategies, MediBuddy can improve revenue, reduce risk exposure, and offer fair pricing to customers."],"metadata":{"id":"pASKb0qOza21"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# **Conclusion**"],"metadata":{"id":"gCX9965dhzqZ"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["The project successfully analyzed MediBuddy’s insurance dataset to identify key factors affecting medical insurance charges.\n","\n","Exploratory Data Analysis revealed that age, BMI, smoking habits, and number of dependents have a significant impact on insurance costs.\n","\n","Factors such as gender and region were found to have minimal influence on insurance charges.\n","\n","Various visualizations including histograms, bar charts, scatter plots, and pair plots helped in understanding data patterns and relationships clearly.\n","\n","The analysis showed that customers with higher age, higher BMI, and smoking habits tend to incur higher medical expenses.\n","\n","These insights can help MediBuddy design better pricing strategies and customer segmentation models.\n","\n","The findings also support risk-based policy planning, helping to reduce financial loss.\n","\n","Overall, the project demonstrates how data-driven analysis can improve decision-making in the healthcare insurance industry."],"metadata":{"id":"Fjb1IsQkh3yE"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["### ***Hurrah! You have successfully completed your EDA Capstone Project !!!***"],"metadata":{"id":"gIfDvo9L0UH2"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":[],"metadata":{"id":"dYX880etpL0x"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":[],"metadata":{"id":"-6Vl263upPVI"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]}]}